//? Title: Context encoders: visible alternating inpainting
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
An image has a missing central region,and its surrounding pixels must support a plausible reconstruction. Stable adversarial losses,mask geometry and hole-only scoring precede complete generator/adversary graphs and actual CIFAR examples. Explicit alternating Adam,phase-isolated BN and generator-only restoration make the short experiment inspectable.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.8_other_vision_tasks/context_encoder.cpp`.

> The method

A generator maps one masked RGB image to a half-side center patch. Its learned
encoder compresses visible context to a1x1 bottleneck;the decoder expands that
representation without skip links. A discriminator learns to separate observed
from generated patches. Reconstruction and non-saturating adversarial losses
supply complementary gradients. The mask determines the information available
at inference;clean targets appear only in training losses and evaluation.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/context_encoder_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/context_encoder_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/context_encoder_concept.tikz > build/context_encoder_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/context_encoder_concept.svg build/context_encoder_concept.dvi > build/context_encoder_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
