> Execute both complete graphs

The reference128-to64 generator has five stride2 encoder stages,a1x1 latent
bottleneck and learned transpose-convolution decoder. The compact32-to16
graph retains three encoder downs,the bottleneck and three decoder stages.
There are no skip links. Encoder/adversary use LeakyReLU(.2),decoder ReLU,
output tanh;BN follows all but the first down and final output.
```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  std::print("| graph | generator learned | discriminator learned | G/D BN scalars | G/D "
             "gradient tensors |\n|---|---:|---:|---|---|\n");
  for (bool compact : {false, true}) {
    n::ParameterStore g(71), gs(72), d(73), ds(74);
    const auto cfg = compact ? m::ContextConfig::Compact() : m::ContextConfig{};
    const auto input =
        (.8 * n::sin(n::arange(0, 4 * cfg.side * cfg.side * 3, 1, n::DType::Float64) * .17))
            .to(n::DType::Float32)
            .reshape({4, cfg.side, cfg.side, 3});
    const auto gen = m::ContextEncoder(g, gs, input, cfg, true, false);
    const auto disc = m::ContextDiscriminator(d, ds, gen.patch, cfg, true, false);
    const auto gg = n::grad(n::mean(n::square(gen.patch)), g.parameters(), {true});
    const auto dg = n::grad(m::ContextBCE(disc.logits, false), d.parameters());
    for (const auto &grads : {gg, dg})
      for (const auto &v : grads)
        if (!n::all(n::less(n::abs(v), INFINITY)).item<bool>())
          return 1;
    if (compact) {
      for (const auto &grads : {gg, dg})
        for (const auto &v : grads)
          if (n::sum(n::square(v.to(n::DType::Float64))).item() == 0)
            return 1;
    }
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {}/{} | {}/{} |\n", compact ? "compact32" : "reference128",
               g.count(), d.count(), gs.count(), ds.count(), gg.size(), dg.size());
  }
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| graph | generator learned | discriminator learned | G/D BN scalars | G/D gradient tensors |
|---|---:|---:|---|---|
| reference128 | 7221231 | 2766529 | 4040/1792 | 40/16 |
| compact32 | 22523 | 2745 | 160/32 | 24/8 |
// result_end

> Actual CIFAR images and the information boundary

The fitting subset is training rows0–127,validation rows128–159;held-out
images are official-test rows160–191. All three sets are disjoint by source
split/row. Original CIFAR binary byte tensors enter Float32 normalization and
masking directly. The hole is filled with(117,104,123)/255 before scaling to
[-1,1]. Generator deployment receives only this masked image.

Use the existing official CIFAR cache at `DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR/cifar10` or
`$XDG_CACHE_HOME/datamunge/datasets/cifar10`(otherwise `~/.cache/...`).
Both `data_batch_1.bin` and `test_batch.bin` are required. No class labels enter
the reconstruction objective. The mean-fill reference has no fitted parameters:
it computes each image’s visible-context mean independently.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/context_encoder_inputs.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <numeric>
#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);

  std::filesystem::path cache;
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR"))
    cache = p;
  else if (const auto *p = std::getenv("XDG_CACHE_HOME"))
    cache = std::filesystem::path(p) / "datamunge/datasets";
  else
    cache = std::filesystem::path(std::getenv("HOME")) / ".cache/datamunge/datasets";
  dm::datasets::fetch("cifar10", (cache / "cifar10").string());

  const auto raw =
      n::data::LoadCifar({cache / "cifar10/data_batch_1.bin"}, n::data::Cifar::k10);
  const auto test_raw =
      n::data::LoadCifar({cache / "cifar10/test_batch.bin"}, n::data::Cifar::k10);
  std::vector<std::size_t> fit_ids(128), val_ids(32), test_ids(32);
  std::iota(fit_ids.begin(), fit_ids.end(), 0);
  std::iota(val_ids.begin(), val_ids.end(), 128);
  std::iota(test_ids.begin(), test_ids.end(), 160);
  const auto fit = m::ContextPairs(raw.images, fit_ids),
             validation = m::ContextPairs(raw.images, val_ids),
             test = m::ContextPairs(test_raw.images, test_ids);

  const auto first = m::InpaintBatch(fit, {0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7});
  const auto mean = m::ContextFillMean(first);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::save_image_grid(m::ContextPreviewTiles(first, mean, mean),
                     "build/context_encoder_inputs.png", 1, 0, 1, 0, 0, 3);
  std::print("Fitting/validation/test images {}/{}/{};valid samples per image {};each "
             "row:masked|mean|mean repeated|truth|4x red mean error.\n",
             fit.truth.size(0), validation.truth.size(0), test.truth.size(0),
             n::sum(n::select(first.valid, 0, 0)).item());
}
```
