// result_end
\caption(Forty-eight explicit alternating D/G Adam updates each. Paired generator and BN checkpoints are selected by validation reconstruction,while adversarial objectives remain visible.)
\alttext(Forty-eight explicit alternating D/G Adam updates each. Paired generator and BN checkpoints are selected by validation reconstruction,while adversarial objectives remain visible.)


\image(figures/context_encoder_metrics.svg)
\caption(Hole-focused metrics over all32 held-out CIFAR images. Both learned reconstruction and the deterministic visible-context mean preserve observed pixels;full-image PSNR is reported separately.)
\alttext(Learned and visible-mean missing-region MSE and mean per-image PSNR.)

\image(figures/context_encoder_predictions.png)
\caption(All32 held-out images,two five-panel tiles per row. Within each tile:masked input,visible-context mean,learned reconstruction,clean truth,and four-times absolute red-channel error. Native tests independently verify every tile pixel.)
\alttext(Actual held-out masked CIFAR images and generated center patches compared with a visible-only reference and clean targets.)

The learned output has lower average hole MSE(.052763 versus .059099),
while the mean-fill reference has slightly higher mean per-image PSNR
(13.411761 versus13.375851dB). These aggregates can disagree because PSNR
averages logarithms of individual image errors. Both full-image PSNR scores
are6.0206dB higher than their hole-only scores.

A decreasing training objective establishes optimization,not high-quality
semantic reconstruction. The small center-hole fit and32px images are a
teaching experiment,not the paper’s ImageNet benchmark. A visible-only
reference can outperform the learned generator;the error galleries and
hole-only metrics expose this directly. No pretrained weights are used.

> Conclusion

Tensor masks,stable losses and independent Jacobian checks establish the local mechanism. Complete graphs and visible alternating optimizer loops then fit actual images. Paired BN restoration and immutable generator-only deployment preserve the information boundary;hole metrics and a strong visible-only reference show the short fit’s limits.

> References

- [Pathak et al.(2016),Context Encoders:Feature Learning by Inpainting](https://arxiv.org/abs/1604.07379).
- [Original context-encoder training implementation](https://github.com/pathak22/context-encoder/blob/master/train.lua).
- [Liu et al.(2018),Image Inpainting for Irregular Holes Using Partial Convolutions](https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.07723).
